Limit: the daemon's own refusals are not covered here — a non-owner connection, a generation that does not match, a spent nonce are the daemon's to make and are covered where it makes them
Limit: a malformed argument throws rather than returning a code, which is agentctl's established contract: the entry point turns a throw into exit 1 with the message on stderr
Ruled-out: offering a role argument | the daemon fixes the role to PRIMARY_CTO and refuses any other, so it would only invite a refused request and restate a fact the daemon already owns
Ruled-out: an --approved=false spelling | a rejection is expressed by not running the command, which is the reason binding recover-dead gives in place
Warn: parse the generation as an integer with a minimum of 1 rather than forwarding the argv token — the daemon reads it with requiredOperatorInteger and refuses a string, producing a refusal the owner cannot diagnose from their side
